# A module may name a function after a type one of its imports exports. The two
# are different namespaces and `kanso check` has always said so.
#
# Until 2026-09-16 the loader did not. `check::declared_names` hands back one
# flat set of type names and function names, `qualify` built its spelling map
# from that set, and this module's `entry` therefore rewrote the bare `entry`
# TYPE that std/json exports -- in a constructor pattern -- to a name no type
# table has ever held. The interpreter ran this program correctly and the
# native backend answered `error: native backend: unknown type
# `<module>/entry``, which is a silent divergence with an internal error for a
# diagnostic.
#
# The corpus runs every fixture through the harness's generated entry, so this
# file reaches the import path the bug lived on.
import "std/json"

pub play = print "{entry 1} {length (json/decode "[1]")}"

fn entry i
  i + 1
